# Where the clock looks for a newer version of itself.
#
# A component Kconfig rather than main's Kconfig.projbuild: this is a
# property of the update component, not of the project, and putting it
# here keeps the option next to the code that reads it.

menu "NN20Clock updates"

    config NN20CLOCK_OTA_MANIFEST_URL
        string "Release manifest URL"
        default "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/brunokeymolen/videoalarmclock/main/latest.json"
        help
            The JSON document naming the current release: its version,
            one line of notes, the image URL, its size, and its SHA-256.
            See nn20clock_ota.h for the shape.

            It lives in the public `videoalarmclock` repository, which
            holds no source - only the firmware binaries, the printable
            base, and the container that converts and uploads video.

            Must be https. The manifest decides which image the clock
            installs, so it is exactly the thing that must not be
            fetched over a channel anyone on the path can rewrite; the
            component refuses a URL that is not, and so does the image
            URL inside it.

            An empty string turns the feature off: the About screen then
            reports that this build has nowhere to check.

endmenu
